  "result": "I've written the revised record to `record.jsonl`; it hasn't been run through the gate yet. The `branch_4` failure came from how the record read the NRS 484B.413(2) composition, not from the coder's code.\n\n**Why `branch_4` came out compliant.** NRS_484B_413_2 only engages at the moment the vehicle's heading first turns to the left of the direction of a lane it is in. In the coder's scene that never happens:\n- At k=17 the subject still points east, along its own lane.\n- At k=18 it points north while in the westbound lane, so it is not pointing along that lane's direction and the left-turn test fails.\n\nSo 413 was never engaged, and a rule that isn't engaged counts as complied. The record made this worse by reading 413 only at the instants the body is across the line. In a real left turn the heading starts turning before the body crosses, so the record would almost never have caught a 413 violation.\n\n**Changes in the record:**\n- **Where 413 is read.** The words tie 413's check to the vehicle's change of course for this turn (\"prior to changing the course\"). E4 now looks back over `p.vehicle_turn_window` from the crossing, finds the last moment 413 engaged (the start of the course change), and requires 413 to be complied with there. If 413 engaged nowhere in that window, the requirement is met; if the window reaches back before the recording starts, the result is unknown.\n- **The coder's turn-target fix, now in the record.** The coder used `st.on_way` to tie the turn's target (the intersection or driveway) to the zone's highway, but the record didn't list it. `st.on_way` and `st.highway` are now in the s10 element, with the justification that a left turn across this highway's striping leaves this highway at a place on it.\n- **Scenarios.** In `branch_1` and `branch_4`, `asm.business_or_residence_district` is declared true; without it 413 returns unknown, not violated. The heading now turns left while the subject is still in its own lane, before the crossing. In `branch_4` the indicator comes on only 10 m before that course change, so 413 is violated even though a signal was on at the observation before the crossing.\n- **Tidying.** `int.left_turn` now reuses the catalogue id without restating its meaning. The parameter proposals are dropped because all six are already in the catalogue.\n\n**Edge case:** if the turn's own course change isn't recognised (for example, the subject is in no mapped lane), the look-back can pick up an earlier, unrelated course change within the turn window.",
